        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Viewing strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access permitted. Please use the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a viewing.\r\n\r\nThis substantial detached country home is situated in Arderrawinny, near Schull, County Cork. Built by its present owner in the late 1990s, the property has remained in single ownership since its construction.\r\nSet amid West Cork’s spectacular landscape, the property enjoys sweeping views across open countryside and towards Dunmanus Bay.\r\nStanding on approximately 1.46 acres in total, the property offers excellent potential for keeping ponies, pursuing a more self-sufficient lifestyle, or creating a smallholding. With the addition of solar panels and other suitable systems, it may also lend itself to off-grid living.\r\nThe property is accessed through a gated entrance framed by attractive stone pillars, with a private driveway leading to the residence.\r\nA particular highlight is the property’s peaceful rural setting, complemented by exceptional views from both the house and its grounds.\r\nLOCATION\r\nThe location combines countryside privacy with convenient access to some of West Cork’s most attractive towns and villages.\r\nSchull is approximately 8 kilometres away, or around a 10 to 15-minute drive.\r\nThis lively and picturesque harbour village offers shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday services, together with a strong sailing tradition, beautiful waterfront walks and a friendly community atmosphere.\r\nBallydehob is approximately 17 kilometres away, or around 20 minutes by car.\r\nKnown for its colourful streets, creative community, galleries, live music and festivals, Ballydehob is a wonderfully characterful village. Its famous 12-arch bridge provides an impressive backdrop overlooking the estuary.\r\nGoleen is approximately 12 kilometres away, or around a 15-minute drive.\r\nThis charming village on the Mizen Peninsula is surrounded by dramatic coastal scenery and provides convenient access to Barleycove Beach, Mizen Head and some of the finest landscapes along the Wild Atlantic Way.\r\nBantry is approximately 34 kilometres away, or around a 40-minute drive.\r\nSet at the head of beautiful Bantry Bay, this vibrant market town provides an excellent selection of shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants and essential services. Bantry is also known for its attractive harbour, historic Bantry House, popular Friday market and renowned music and cultural events.\r\nCork City is approximately 115 kilometres away, with a driving time of around one hour and 50 minutes.\r\nThe city offers major shopping facilities, hospitals, universities, excellent restaurants and an extensive selection of cultural and historical attractions, including the celebrated English Market.\r\nCork Airport is approximately 110 kilometres away, or around one hour and 45 minutes by car.\r\nThe airport provides convenient connections to a broad selection of destinations throughout the United Kingdom and Europe.\r\nACCOMMODATION\r\nThe accommodation is arranged over two floors and extends to a total recorded floor area of approximately 195.96 square metres\r\nThe ground-floor accommodation includes an entrance hallway, utility room, kitchen, separate dining room, spacious front reception room, office/bonus room and a bathroom.\r\nThe first floor contains four bedrooms, two private en-suite shower rooms, a main family bathroom, an upstairs hallway and a hot press.\r\nGROUND FLOOR\r\nENTRANCE HALLWAY\r\nApproximately 4.1m × 2.7m\r\n13'5\" × 8'10\"\r\nThe entrance hallway provides access to the principal ground-floor rooms and features a traditional timber staircase leading to the first floor.\r\nUTILITY ROOM\r\nApproximately 3.4m × 3.3m\r\n11'2\" × 10'10\"\r\nThe practical utility room includes laundry facilities, fitted storage, worktop space and access to the rear entrance area.\r\nKITCHEN\r\nApproximately 4.2m × 6.3m\r\n13'9\" × 20'8\"\r\nThe generously proportioned kitchen features extensive timber cabinetry, plentiful work surfaces, integrated cooking facilities and windows overlooking the surrounding countryside.\r\nDINING ROOM\r\nThe separate dining room provides a welcoming family space with a feature fireplace, timber ceiling and glazed doors opening directly onto the garden.\r\nFRONT RECEPTION ROOM\r\nApproximately 5.5m × 4.2m\r\n18'1\" × 13'9\"\r\nThe spacious front reception room features a striking period-style fireplace, timber ceiling, multiple windows and glazed doors opening onto the garden.\r\nOFFICE/BONUS ROOM\r\nApproximately 3.0m × 4.2m\r\n9'10\" × 13'9\"\r\nThis flexible ground-floor room is suitable for use as a home office, study, playroom, hobby room or general-purpose bonus room.\r\nGROUND-FLOOR BATHROOM\r\nApproximately 3.5m × 1.2m\r\n11'6\" × 3'11\"\r\nThe ground-floor bathroom includes a bath, wash-hand basin and toilet.\r\nFIRST FLOOR\r\nUPSTAIRS HALLWAY\r\nApproximately 2.7m × 5.6m\r\n8'10\" × 18'4\"\r\nThe spacious first-floor hallway provides access to all four bedrooms, the main bathroom and the hot press.\r\nFRONT LEFT BEDROOM\r\nApproximately 4.5m × 3.0m\r\n14'9\" × 9'10\"\r\nA bright and generously proportioned bedroom with attractive views of the surrounding countryside.\r\nBACK LEFT BEDROOM\r\nApproximately 3.1m × 4.2m\r\n10'2\" × 13'9\"\r\nA comfortable double bedroom offering generous floor space and natural light.\r\nBACK RIGHT BEDROOM\r\nApproximately 4.1m × 4.2m\r\n13'5\" × 13'9\"\r\nA generously sized bedroom benefiting from its own private en-suite shower room.\r\nBACK RIGHT EN-SUITE\r\nApproximately 1.2m × 1.9m\r\n3'11\" × 6'3\"\r\nThe en-suite includes a shower, wash-hand basin and toilet.\r\nFRONT RIGHT BEDROOM\r\nApproximately 4.2m × 3.0m\r\n13'9\" × 9'10\"\r\nA bright double bedroom with its own private en-suite shower room.\r\nFRONT RIGHT EN-SUITE\r\nApproximately 1.2m × 2.1m\r\n3'11\" × 6'11\"\r\nThe en-suite includes a shower, wash-hand basin and toilet.\r\nFIRST-FLOOR BATHROOM\r\nApproximately 2.8m × 2.8m\r\n9'2\" × 9'2\"\r\nThe main first-floor bathroom provides additional bathroom facilities for the remaining bedrooms.\r\nHOT PRESS\r\nApproximately 2.8m × 1.0m\r\n9'2\" × 3'3\"\r\nThe hot press provides useful storage space on the first floor.\r\nTOTAL FLOOR AREA\r\nApproximately 195.96 square metres\r\nFor further information or to arrange a viewing, please contact the selling agent.\r\nPROPERTY INFORMATION & CONTACT DETAILS\r\nProperty Type: Detached country home\r\nAddress: Arderrawinny, Schull, County Cork\r\nEircode: P81 PC82\r\nSite Area: Approximately 1.46 acres\r\nBedrooms: Four\r\nBathrooms: Four, including two en-suite shower rooms\r\nTenure: Freehold\r\nBER: C\r\nBER No.: 112302179\r\nEnergy Performance Indicator: 177.20 kWh/m²/yr\r\nMain Energy Carrier: Heating oil\r\n____________________________________\r\nSelling Agent: Irish Rural Homes\r\nContact: Mary Cotter \r\nTelephone: 085 935 9250\r\nEmail: irishruralhomes@gmail.com\r\nPSRA Licence No: 002675\r\n\r\nGeneral Disclaimer / Important Notice\r\nThese particulars are issued by Irish Rural Homes for guidance purposes only and do not form part of any contract. While every effort has been made to ensure accuracy, all descriptions, measurements, floor plans, boundaries, photographs, services, planning information and other details are approximate and should not be relied upon as statements of fact.\r\nInterested parties should satisfy themselves fully as to the condition, title, boundaries, planning status, services, fixtures, fittings and all other matters relating to the property prior to entering into any contract. The property, lands and any outbuildings are offered as seen, and no warranty is given by the vendor or selling agent in relation to their condition, suitability, use or future development potential.\r\nViewing is strictly by appointment only. No unauthorised access is permitted to the dwelling, lands or farm buildings. Please contact Irish Rural Homes using the contact details provided in this listing to arrange a suitable viewing time."
      },
